    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2019-boundary-09: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.08";
    dc:description "The claim reframes whose interests cellular behavior serves rather than predicting a distinct observation. Information flow can be mapped, but it cannot establish equality of selfishness or uniquely identify the proposed Self.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Information-flow range and cooperative behavior could be measured, but describing all cells as equally selfish and assigning the beneficiary as the relevant Self is definitional rather than an independently testable consequence.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Selfishness and Self are redefined to make the statement hold.", "The same data permit non-agentic descriptions.";
